<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Module 8 Worksheet</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1e293b;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 40px auto;
    max-width: 800px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #0f172a;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #7b4fce;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  h2, h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #7b4fce;
    margin-top: 35px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-left: 4px solid #00c8ff;
    padding-left: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: #334155;
  }
  ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    padding-left: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  li {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .checkbox {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-family: monospace;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-right: 10px;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .instructions {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #475569;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .question {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .response-box {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px dashed #7b4fce;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    margin: 10px 0 25px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #475569;
  }
  .response-label {
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #7b4fce;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  .response-placeholder {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PlayIQ Module 8 Worksheet: Writing, Outlines, and Revision</h1>
<div class="instructions"><strong>Instructions:</strong> Complete this worksheet thoughtfully. Remember, PlayIQ is about using AI as a coach, not a crutch. Your goal is to become an independent learner!</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 1: Claim, Evidence, Reasoning</h3>
<div class="question">1. (Short Response) What do the three letters in C.E.R. stand for?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">2. (Multiple Choice) In the CER framework, what is the "Reasoning"?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> What you think or answer.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> The facts or data that support your answer.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Why the evidence proves the claim.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> The introduction paragraph.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">3. (Classification) Read this sentence: "The plant grew taller because it was placed in the sun, which shows that sunlight provides necessary energy for growth." Which part is the Claim, which is the Evidence, and which is the Reasoning?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">4. (Teach-Back) Explain how using Claim, Evidence, Reasoning (CER) makes your writing stronger than just giving an opinion.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 2: Outline First</h3>
<div class="question">5. (Short Response) Why does outlining prevent messy writing?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">6. (Multiple Choice) What should an outline do?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Replace your thinking entirely.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Guide your answer so you don't get stuck.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Write the essay for you.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Confuse the reader.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">7. (Prompt Improvement) You need to write a paragraph about climate change. Write a prompt asking AI to help you make a simple outline, making sure to ask the AI *not* to write the final paragraph for you.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">8. (Scenario) You spend 5 minutes making an outline with your AI coach before writing your essay. Your friend starts writing immediately without an outline. Halfway through, your friend gets stuck and doesn't know what to write next. How did your outline protect you from this?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 3: Feedback Prompt System</h3>
<div class="question">9. (Short Response) What is the difference between "good AI feedback" and "bad AI feedback"?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">10. (Multiple Choice) Which of the following is an example of specific, good feedback?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> "Make this better."</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> "This sounds weird."</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> "Your second paragraph is missing a clear transition sentence to connect it to the third paragraph."</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> "Rewrite the whole thing."</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">11. (Prompt Improvement) You want feedback on an essay. Instead of saying "Fix my essay," write a prompt asking the AI to review it for clarity, logic, and missing evidence, and ask it to give you *3 specific suggestions*.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">12. (Scenario) The AI gives you 3 suggestions. You only agree with 2 of them, so you ignore the third one. Is this allowed? Why does this keep you in control as the writer?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">13. (Teach-Back) Teach someone how to ask AI for *specific* feedback on their writing instead of asking AI to just "fix it."</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 4: Revision Loop</h3>
<div class="question">14. (Short Response) What does "revision" actually mean? Why does it not mean letting AI replace your voice?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">15. (Multiple Choice) A strong revision:</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Changes all of your words into big, confusing vocabulary.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Keeps your meaning but makes it clearer.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Deletes your ideas and replaces them with AI ideas.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Means you never have to check your work.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">16. (Classification) You write a paragraph. You ask AI to revise it. The AI rewrites it, and it sounds like a college professor wrote it, not a 7th grader. Is this a strong revision, or did the AI steal your voice? What should you do?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">17. (Scenario) You revise your answer based on AI feedback. You then ask the AI to compare your first version to your revised version. Why is this comparison step important for your brain?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">18. (Teach-Back) Explain the difference between revising your own work with AI coaching, versus letting AI ghostwrite the answer for you.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">19. (Reflection) Think of a time you turned in a first draft without revising it. If you had used the AI Feedback Prompt System, what is one thing that probably would have improved?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">20. (Reflection) What is one writing habit (like outlining, or checking your reasoning) that you want to keep using in the future?</div>
